# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12 (Q45): a method's call in a named Structure's body is a statement of the
# body, as in a method's body -- put, declared above, adds 5 to the unit's seen; later, declared below
# (methods are visible both ways), takes n and adds it to the unit's last.  Two executions from the root:
# seen 10, n 1 (its declaration runs again), last 2.  Entry 7.
size_t: seen 0U
size_t: last 0U
fn: put (size_t: a) int
    seen: seen + a
return: 0
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    put: 5U
    n: n + 1U
    later: n
return
fn: later (size_t: v) int
    last: last + v
return: 0
Counter
Counter
int: ok 0
if: seen = 10U && Counter\n = 1U && last = 2U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
